# skyeLoch -- Garbhán, on the loch's island
#
# Format: the English line, then `% the Irish` under it.
#   plain lines = Garbhán's opening card;  > = the hero;  < = Garbhán's answers.
#   Lines in a row (> > or < <) share one turn; a new > starts the next turn.

@file skye/skyeLoch
@encounter 0

# ══ first meeting ══════════════════════════════════════════════
= first meeting
@when !note garbhan_met
And where is it, o little grey sparrow
% Agus cá háit, a gealbhan beag liath

< do you think to fly today?
% a ceapann tú eitilt inniu?
> To the tournament. 
% Go dtí an comórtas.
> I would be grateful if you let me pass, friend.
% Bheinn buíoch dá bhfágfá an bealach a chara.

< Friend! Did ye hear that, water? 
% A chara! An gcuala tú é sin, uisce? 

< Did ye hear that, sky? 
% An gcuala tú é sin, spéir? 
< Friend, says the sparrow. Friend!
% A chara, arsa an gealbhan. A chara!


< Turn back, little one, turn back.
% Cas síar, a chréatúir, cas síar.

< Theres no place in the tournament for the likes of you.
% Níl áit sa comórtas dá leithead.

> That is not your decision.
% Ní fútsa an cinneadh sin.

< Come across then if ye dare it. 
% Tar trasna mar sin má tá an chroí ionat.

< Come and let me have a look at that fine wooden sword.
% Tar go bhfeice mé an claíomh maith adhmaid sin.


> I will go round.
% Rachaidh mé timpeall.

< Ye will not,
% Ní rachaidh tú,

< for I will be there before you.
% óir beidh mise ansin romhat.

< My legs are longer.
% Tá mo chosa níos faide.

> No harm done yet.
% Níl aon dochar deanta fós.

> Stand aside
% Seas ar leataobh
> and I will stand aside in my turn.
% agus seasfaidh mise ar leataobh duitse, lá éigin.


< Is that some charm? A spell, is it?
% An piseog ab ea? Geasróg an ea?

> It is only the gentle word
% Níl ann ach an focal lách

> and the truth
% agus an fhirine

< Well,
% Más ea,

< I've no use for the like.
% Níl aon úsáid agam dá leithead.

< Come try Garbhóg the Thick-Necked!
% Tar is bain triail as Garbhóg an Muineál Mór!

> Come then.
% Tar, mar sin.

# ══ he has had you before ══════════════════════════════════════
= again
@when note garbhan_met
Back again? Good.
% Ar ais arís? Go maith.
